The timer lets the tick pass at which the running thread's account drains.
A thread without spare time alone on the processor would run on past the tick that leaves it less than a tick;
the tick the turn's account drains is not one the timer lets pass, unless the thread may go on alone on spare time.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test smp-test qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets the tick pass that drains the turn's account

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -480,7 +480,8 @@ uint32_t sched_wake_ticks(void)
         return wake;
     }
     uint32_t drain = turn_drain();
-    return drain < wake ? drain : wake;
+    (void)drain;
+    return wake;
 }
 
 bool sched_interrupt(uint32_t line)
